It's also like the mastermind at the castle: a game, a gimmick, a nice
decoration.  One of the features that makes the game interesting.  Not
because *Sokoban* is an interesting game, no.  It's interesting because
NH can incorporate such sub-games with the tools (boulders, traps) that
are (more or less) already present in NH.

BTW, I played "Sokoban" in NH before it had been implemented... 8-)
Others did that too, I am sure.

Monsters using wands of digging in corridors, making it impossible to
proceed to the next level (by "impossible" I mean without the ability
to simply return; you can of course jump into the hole and hope).
In such situations I tried to find boulders to maneuvre them through
the wrickled corridors to plug the hole.

Another application is to move the boulders to have some fortress or
to build a hallway to handle monsters one by one.

Another application is using and moving boulders through Medusas level
to cross the sea.  That is also related to Sokoban; move the boulders
optimally, don't lose one, use as few boulders as possible, choose the
optimal path, don't make a wrong step.

And to close the circle from Medusa to Sokoban here, I appreciate the
guaranteed scrolls of earth in Sokoban, e.g. to use them for Medusas
level (if I have no other means crossing the water).

